### Key Liquiflow Patterns
 
**Promoted section — mixed-block featured area, staging prototype (2026-07-24, revised same day):**
```
li-content-for-blocks                                  ← on .promotion_list-layout; lets merchants mix + reorder both block types below

li-snippet          = Section Header                    ← reused from Team.html's proven pattern, at section top
li-block            = Kicker / Headline                 ← inside the Section Header snippet

li-block            = Promoted Panel
li-settings:custom  = Panel                             ← JSON array: {"type":"collection","id":"collection",...} + {"type":"checkbox","id":"half_width",...}
li-liquid                                               ← REQUIRED on the custom-JSON embed, see fix note below
li-object:href      = block.settings.collection.url
li-object:src       = block.settings.collection.image | image_url: width: 1536
li-object            = block.settings.collection.title

li-block            = Collection Slider
li-settings:text     = Heading                          ← per-instance slider title, e.g. "Gift Guides", "Wedding Picks"
li-settings:collection = Products                       ← merchant picks a collection; auto-loops its products as slides
                                                          ← no half-width setting (Joe: sliders don't need it, removed)

li-attribute:class  = promotion_list-item{% if block.settings.half_width %} is-half{% endif %}   ← Promoted Panel only now
```
Superseded the `promoted`-linklist version (same day — see collections-architecture.md) after Joe asked for panels and sliders to live in one freely-arrangeable area with per-block full/half width control.

**Bug found + fixed (2026-07-30): the entire Panel block had *no settings at all* in the Theme Editor.** Symptom Joe reported: every other section's settings show up in Edit Theme, Promoted's Panel blocks show none. Verified against production's unpublished `Clover` theme (#161621770489), not staging:

- Pulled `sections/promoted.liquid` — the compiled Panel block schema was `{"name":"Panel","type":"panel","settings":[{"type":"header","content":"Panel"}]}`. Header only; `collection`, `video` and `half_width` were gone, while the compiled block markup still referenced `block.settings.collection.url`, `block.settings.video` and `block.settings.half_width`. `templates/index.json` matched: `"panel_WFMzVq": {"type":"panel","settings":{}}`.
- Root cause: the Builder's own save cycle had re-serialized `_sections/Promoted.html` and hard-wrapped the `li-settings:custom` embed **inside two JSON string values** (`"label":"Video\n                (optional, overrides image)"`, `"label":"Half\n                width"`). Raw newlines in a JSON string = invalid JSON → the converter emitted only the attribute-derived header and dropped the array. Silent: no build error, and the Builder's linter doesn't check embed JSON.
- Proof the published theme was built from that corrupted state (not from the valid one-line version in git): the compiled `promoted.liquid` carries the reformatted source's fingerprint — `document.addEventListener` indented 14 spaces, matching the working tree, vs 0 spaces at `HEAD`.
- Fix: JSON rewritten as one object per line, short lines, so a future re-wrap can only break between tokens. Validated with `JSON.parse`. See the gotchas doc for the defensive format.
- **Status: ✅ verified on production.** Joe republished 2026-07-30 22:06 UTC; re-pulled `sections/promoted.liquid` and the Panel block schema now reads `[header, collection, video, half_width]`.
- Correction to the note below: the embed never had `w-embed` in any committed version, and it isn't needed — the converter keys off the attribute. And `li-settings:custom="Panel"`'s value is only a Theme-Editor header label, not an id.

**Bug found + "fixed" (2026-07-24), causal claim now doubted: half-width setting didn't work in the Theme Editor.** Root cause claimed at the time: the `li-settings:custom` JSON embed (documented then as `` — the `w-embed` part was never actually in the file) had no `li-liquid` attribute. Per `docs/liquid-attributes/miscellaneous`: "Webflow may alter the formatting of certain characters — especially double quotes — within Custom Code elements... apply `li-liquid` to preserve original formatting during export." Without it, Webflow's export mangled the JSON's quotes, so the custom setting silently failed to register. **Any `li-settings:custom` JSON embed needs `li-liquid` alongside it** — add this to the gotchas doc too.

Used `li-settings:custom` (raw Shopify schema JSON) instead of the native `li-settings:collection`/`li-settings:checkbox` convenience modifiers for **Promoted Panel**'s fields specifically — those modifiers auto-generate a `<modifier>_<handleized-label>` setting id (confirmed via docs: `li-settings:image="Image"` → `section.settings.image_image`), which isn't dot-notation-safe for hyphenated labels and isn't confirmed to give a plain single-collection reference outside the documented "product item" loop use case. Custom JSON sidesteps both problems with explicit, predictable `id`s.

**Section Header, added 2026-07-24**: Joe wanted slider blocks to carry more than a heading. Considered nesting the Section Header snippet's Kicker/Headline `li-block`s *inside* the Collection Slider block, but skipped it — no documented confirmation that Liquiflow's dynamic `li-content-for-blocks` system supports a `li-block` nested inside another `li-block` (the one documented nested-blocks case, "repeated up to 8 times," is specific to the separate *static* theme-blocks system, `li-static-block`/`li-cf-theme-blocks`). Went with a single section-level Section Header instead (reusing Team.html's exact proven pattern) — one optional kicker+headline intro for the whole Promoted area, not per-slider.

CSS: `.promotion_list-layout` changed from `flex-flow: column` to `row wrap`; `.promotion_list-item` is `width: 100%` by default, `.is-half` is `calc(50% - gap/2)` above 767px and forced back to full width below it (`css/clover-crane.webflow.css`).

**⚠️ "Verified live on staging (2026-07-24)" — no longer evidence.** Staging is deprecated as a reference (see `site-transfer-reference.md`), and on production the Panel block's settings were in fact absent right through 2026-07-30 (above), so anything below that depended on a merchant-configured `block.settings.collection` was not actually exercised on production. Re-verify after the next publish. Original note follows: `block.settings.collection` correctly resolves a single collection reference (not a forced product loop) — confirmed via two real Promoted Panel blocks (Gifts for Him, Gifts for Her) rendering correctly. Half-width also confirmed working after a follow-up CSS fix: `.promotion_list-layout` was `display:flex` with a `calc(50% - gap/2)` width on `.is-half` — the Builder's own save cycle had added `gap: var(--gap-6)` (a different, larger token than the `--gap-4` the calc was written against), so two half-width items summed just over the container width and wrapped instead of sitting side by side. Switched to CSS Grid (`repeat(2, 1fr)`, full-width items `grid-column: 1/-1`, half-width `span 1`) — grid divides space against whatever gap is actually set, no manual calc to get wrong. Collection Slider and Find Your Store also confirmed rendering correctly with real merchant-configured data.

**Section Header block — tried, rejected by Joe (2026-07-24), removed from source.** The flattened version (single block, plain `li-settings:text` for Kicker + Headline, no nested `li-block`s, not reusing Team.html's `li-snippet`) wasn't the solution Joe was looking for — removed from `_sections/Promoted.html` via the Builder. Not currently planned to come back in this form. May resurface once/if the Group-block work (see below) lands on `li-content-for-theme-blocks`, which would allow genuine nested Kicker/Headline sub-blocks instead of the flattened version — but that's speculative, not a commitment.

