## Sliders — de-webflow migration to Swiper.js (2026-07-24)

Joe pays for Swiper Studio (a Shopify app for merchant-built carousels) and asked whether to install it, or hand-code Swiper.js instead. Recommended hand-coding: `Product Hero.html`'s media gallery already used real Swiper.js successfully (proven pattern to copy), while Home's sliders used Webflow's native `.w-slider` — inconsistent within the same project. Installing Swiper Studio would also have been redundant with the merchant-configurable Collection Slider blocks already built the same day (its whole value-add — app-block carousels merchants configure themselves — is what those blocks already do natively).

**What changed:**
- `_layouts/theme.html` head: added `<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/swiper@11/swiper-bundle.min.js" defer="defer">` once, site-wide (matches the Alpine/Liquify-core/Finsweet pattern already there).
- `_sections/Product Hero.html`: removed its own duplicate `swiper-bundle.min.js` load (was loading it a second time per-page) &mdash; its own init script is unchanged.
- `_sections/Promoted.html`'s Collection Slider block and `_sections/Stores.html`'s Find Your Store slider: rebuilt from Webflow's `.w-slider`/`.w-slide`/`.w-slider-arrow-*` markup to real Swiper structure (`.swiper`/`.swiper-wrapper`/`.swiper-slide`, `.swiper-button-wrapper` + `.swiper-prev`/`.swiper-next`), each with its own `DOMContentLoaded` init script scoped to a distinct class (`cc-promoted-slider`, `cc-store-slider`) so multiple Collection Slider block instances all init correctly and the two sections' init scripts never double-initialize each other's elements.
- `css/clover-crane.webflow.css`: added `overflow: hidden` to `.collection-slider` &mdash; Swiper clips via the `.swiper` element itself, unlike Webflow's slider which used a separate `.w-slider-mask` child for that. `.collection-slider_slide`'s existing `width: 18rem` + `margin-right: var(--gap-4)` was reused as-is (works naturally with Swiper's `slidesPerView: 'auto'` mode &mdash; no `spaceBetween` set in the JS config, to avoid doubling the gap). `.collection-slider_mask` and `.collection-slider_arrow` are now dead CSS (unused, harmless, not cleaned up).
- Reused `.swiper-button`/`.swiper-button-wrapper` CSS verbatim &mdash; already generic (not Product-Hero-scoped), so the new sliders' prev/next buttons get identical chrome/positioning to Product Hero's for free.

**Found in passing, not yet acted on:** `_layouts/theme.html` head also already loads a Swiper Studio-generated bundle (`swiper_studio_sparkling_margalit_681-1.0.3.js`, hosted on Webflow's CDN under this project's site ID) &mdash; Swiper Studio's *Webflow script-embed* integration, not the Shopify App Store listing Joe was asking about. No markup anywhere in the project has matching Swiper-Studio-specific hooks, so it appears orphaned/unused. Left in place &mdash; Joe should confirm nothing depends on it before removing.

All lint-clean. Not yet visually verified on staging &mdash; needs a Builder publish first (same as the earlier Promoted work), then check both sliders actually swipe/paginate correctly.

**Inspiration section (not currently built, see note above) &mdash; linklist-driven, for reference:**
```
