## Product Page (`li-page="product"`)
 
### Sections
| Section | Attribute |
|---|---|
| Product Hero | `li-section="Product Hero"` + `li-section:on_templates="product"` |
| Recommended Products | `li-section="Recommended Products"` + `li-section:on_templates="product"` |
 
### Key Liquiflow Patterns
 
**Theme blocks container:**
```
li-content-for-theme-blocks = (empty value)
```
Applied to `product-hero_info` div &mdash; creates block file container for the section.
 
**Media gallery (Swiper):**
```
li-for:inside = media in product.media
```
> `:inside` modifier renders the loop inside the element rather than wrapping it.
```
li-if = media.media_type == 'image'
li-if = media.media_type == 'video'
li-object:src = media | image_url: width: 1000, height: 1000
li-object = media | video_tag: controls: true
```
 
**Product form:**
```
li-form       = product
li-form:product = (empty value)   &larr; empty = use current page's product context
```
Converts to `{% form 'product', product %}` in Liquid.
 
**Price display:**
```
li-object = product.price | money
li-if     = product.compare_at_price > product.price
li-object = product.compare_at_price | money
```
 
**Availability:**
```
li-if     = product.available      &larr; in-stock row
li-unless = product.available      &larr; out-of-stock row
```
 
**Description:**
```
li-if     = product.description
li-object = product.description
```
 
**FAQ Accordion blocks:**
```
li-block          = Accordion
li-settings:text  = Heading
li-settings:richtext = Content
```
> `li-settings:richtext` creates a formatted rich text field in the Theme Editor.
 
**Recommended products (Section Rendering API &mdash; Alpha):**
```
li-render-recommended              = wrapper
li-render-recommended-product      = {{ product.id }}
li-render-recommended-path         = {{ routes.product_recommendations_url }}
li-render-recommended-intent       = complementary
li-render-recommended-limit        = 8
li-render-recommended              = target
li-for                             = product in recommendations.products
```
> Requires `section-rendering.js` in Shopify theme assets &mdash; already installed via head code.
 
### Fixes Applied
| Fix | Detail |
|---|---|
| Invalid `id` on accordion heading | Removed `id="accordion-heading-{{forloop.index}}"` &mdash; `forloop` is undefined outside a `li-for` loop |
| `li-block` on Add to Cart | Removed `li-block="Add to Cart"` from form group &mdash; Add to Cart should always be visible, not togglable |
| Variant swatches always black | `ccSwatches` was built via `{% for %}`/`{% if %}` in a bare `x-data`, which the Builder can't compile &mdash; moved to `li-attribute:x-data`. See `/docs/liquiflow-rules-and-gotchas.md`. |
| Swatch colors still not showing after the above | `product_option_value.swatch.color`/`.image` returns `nil` on this store despite the Color option being correctly linked to `shopify.color-pattern`. Switched to a direct `metaobjects['shopify--color-pattern'][handle]` lookup &mdash; see gotchas doc for the exact pattern. |
| Personalization checkbox showed no checkmark | The visible `.checkbox-input` div never got Webflow's `w--redirected-checked` class (no native class markers to trigger it). Bound directly to Alpine: `x-bind:class="{ 'w--redirected-checked': personalization }"`. |
| "Select style:"/"Placement:"/"Text color:" missing space after colon | Two adjacent `<span>`s with a literal space text node between them &mdash; the Builder strips whitespace-only text nodes on its own save cycle. Used `&nbsp;` instead. |
| Style/Text-color pickers not hidden when merchant leaves the metafield blank | Added `li-if="product.metafields.custom.monogram_styles != blank"` / `..._text_colors != blank` wrappers, matching the pattern Placement already had. |
| Style list stacked full-width instead of wrapping; Placement not a 3&times;3 grid | Both used bare `li-for` on the container div instead of `li-for:inside` &mdash; see gotchas doc. CSS (`.product_radio-list` flex-wrap, `.monogram_placement-grid`) was already correct. |
| Style image showed broken-image icon when unset | Added `li-if="style.style_image"` on the `<img>`. |
| No indication of current selection ("Select style: Default" never changed) | Added `selectedStyle`/`selectedPlacement`/`selectedColor` to the `#monogram` `x-data`, `x-model` + `type="radio"` on each option input (radios were missing `type="radio"` entirely &mdash; plain text inputs), and `x-text="selectedX || 'Not set'"` on each label. |
| Text-color swatch label showed wrong/broken text | Its `<label>` had a leftover `x-init="optionValue = selected_or_first_available_variant..."` copy-pasted from the main Color variant swatch &mdash; those Alpine variables don't exist in this scope. Removed it. |
| Style radios would have rendered blank (found 2026-07-30) | Markup read `style.label` but production's `monogram_style` definition uses the key **`style_label`** &mdash; empty label, empty image alt, empty `properties[Design]` on the order. Fixed all three reads to `style.style_label`. Metaobject field keys are immutable, so markup is what moves. `collections-architecture.md`'s field table (which said `label`) was the source of the drift and is now corrected. |
| Monogram text limit was hardcoded to 3 characters (changed 2026-07-30) | `maxlength="3"` and the literal "Add text (2 or 3 characters)" label meant every style shared one limit, and the existing `custom.monogram_max_characters` product metafield was referenced nowhere. Now per-style: added a `max_characters` integer field to the `monogram_style` metaobject (production, 2026-07-30), each style radio carries `li-attribute:data-max="{{ style.max_characters }}"` and an `x-on:change` that sets `maxChars` (falling back to `defaultMax`) and truncates any text already typed; the input binds `x-bind:maxlength="maxChars"` + `x-model="monogramText"` and the label is `x-text`-driven. Precedence: style value &rarr; product `monogram_max_characters` &rarr; 3. The `#monogram` `x-data` moved to `li-attribute:x-data` because it now seeds those defaults from Liquid (per the gotchas doc's bare-`x-data` rule). Client-side only &mdash; nothing validates the line item property server-side. |
| Duplicate `name` attribute on Placement input | Had both `name="Placement"` and `li-attribute:name="properties[Placement]"` on the same element (invalid HTML &mdash; undefined which wins). Kept only the dynamic one, matching the Style/Color inputs' plain `name="properties[...]"` convention. |

