## Collection Page (`li-page="collection"`)

### Sections
| Section | Attribute |
|---|---|
| Basic Hero (Dynamic) | `li-section="Basic Hero (Dynamic)"` &mdash; title/description hero, clean, no issues found |
| Collection Products | `li-section="Collection Products"` + `li-section:on_templates="collection"` &mdash; filter sidebar, product grid, pagination |

### Key Liquiflow Patterns

**Product card, reused via `li-snippet` (also called from `_sections/Promoted.html`'s home-page Collection Slider &mdash; see Home Page section):**
```
li-snippet          = product-card
li-snippet:product  = product
```
> Both call sites must stay byte-identical &mdash; `li-snippet` dedupes by name, not by call site.

**AJAX collection filtering (Section Rendering API &mdash; Alpha):**
```
li-render-filter = wrapper        &larr; on the container wrapping filters + product list
li-render-filter = filter         &larr; on each filter checkbox/radio
li-render-filter-value = {{ filter_value.value }}
li-render-filter-name  = {{ filter_value.param_name }}
li-render-filter = filter-remove  &larr; on the "remove this filter" tag
li-render-filter-value = {{ filter_value.url_to_remove }}
li-render-filter = sort           &larr; on the sort <select>
li-render-filter = clear-all      &larr; on the "clear all filters" button
```
> `li-render-filter-value`/`li-render-filter-name` are dedicated attributes the filter JS reads &mdash; **not** `li-attribute:value`/`li-attribute:name`. See Fixes Applied below; also flags a linter false positive, see `/CLAUDE.md` &rarr; Key Learnings.

### Fixes Applied (2026-07-24 audit)
| Fix | Detail |
|---|---|
| Filter checkboxes silently did nothing | Used `li-attribute:value`/`li-attribute:name` instead of the documented `li-render-filter-value`/`li-render-filter-name`. The AJAX filter script reads the latter specifically &mdash; the checkboxes weren't wired to it at all. Fixed both, and the "remove filter" tag's `li-attribute:href` &rarr; `li-render-filter-value` the same way. |
| Filter checkbox `id` didn't match its label's `for` | `id` was a bare, unwrapped attribute embedding `{{ }}` (`id="filter-{{ ... }}"`) &mdash; the Builder can't compile Liquid in a bare attribute, so it rendered literally and never matched the label's already-correct `li-attribute:for`. Fixed to `li-attribute:id`. |
| Variant data possibly not reaching `handleVariant()` on product cards | Same bare-attribute-with-embedded-Liquid bug as the Product Hero `ccSwatches` incident &mdash; `x-data="handleVariant({{ product \| json \| escape }}, ...)"` was a plain attribute, not `li-attribute:x-data`. Fixed. |
| Product card preview link's accessible name rendered literally as `View {{ product.title }}` | Same bug, on a bare `aria-label`. Fixed to `li-attribute:aria-label`. |
| Linter false positive on the filter attribute fix above | See `/CLAUDE.md` Key Learnings &mdash; `li-render-filter`/`li-render-filter-value`/`li-render-filter-name` on one element trips `STANDALONE_CONFLICT`, but is the documented required pattern. Do not revert. |

Minor/not fixed: pagination's "Previous" button has a stray bare `id` attribute with no value (Webflow export debris, cosmetic, harmless).

